     "result_text_tail": " pack or are calculated from it, with no placeholders left. The briefing pack writes \"two of the three cities\" as words, so the automatic match between that number (2) and its quote can't run. I checked it by hand.\n\n**Decisions I made for you**\n- **Audience:** the board deciding to approve or reject the launch.\n- **Theme:** `navy`.\n- **Storyline:** I approved it myself.\n- **Two exec-summary bullets cut to one sub-point each** so the page reads at full size.\n- **The $9.5M:** I read it as the company's full cash need to month 18, the reading most favourable to the founders. If it covers only the launch, today's $0.4M monthly burn comes on top and cash runs out before month 18. A footnote on that slide says so.\n- **\"Contribution per order\"** is after dark-store costs and before head-office costs, capex and customer acquisition. The pack doesn't say how the incumbents define it; that is footnoted too.\n\n**Things the board should know**\n- Even without a launch, today's burn leaves exactly 12 months of runway at month 18. New software contracts have to pay for the hires, so I added a next step for the CFO to set a burn plan.\n- The $3.6M pipeline figure is an upper bound, because the pack gives no win rates.\n\nTo edit, change `work/build_spec.py` and re-run it with `check.py` and `render.py`; the spec it writes is `work/parcelbird-now.json`. I can also switch the theme (for example `mono` for printing) or add a short appendix with the full per-order calculation for each set of inputs."
